  "_comment": "Signora's demonstration cast, WITH THE PEOPLE AT EACH COMPANY. Successor to playground@3, which is identical in every company, domain, country, industry, founding year, headcount, revenue band and stage — the only change is that each company's 'contact_titles' has become 'people', where every contact now has a NAME. EVERY PERSON HERE IS INVENTED, at a company that is also invented, and neither is intended to be or to resemble any real individual or business (TASK-429, TASK-1480). This is why the named cast could not land on playground@2: its twelve entities were REAL companies, and an invented individual with an invented stance attached to a real employer is a fabricated claim about a real business AND about a real person's employer. A new version rather than an edit because a published dataset is immutable — every recorded run cites a content hash, and mutating @3 would make TASK-1480's evidence describe a dataset that no longer exists.",
